<title>USA: Rockwell to flood market with new chips - WSJ.</title>
<headline>Rockwell to flood market with new chips - WSJ.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rockwell International Corp's Semiconductor Systems division is hoping to flood the market with millions of chips in the next few months to gain an edge in highspeed computer modem industry, the Wall Street Journal said Monday.</p>
<p>Dwight Decker, president of the company's Semiconductor Systems division, said in an interview that more than 100,000 modem chips will be sent by late February and that three million or more chip sets could be shipped by midyear.</p>
<p>The report said the rollout would be much faster than expected and is a strike against rival U.S. Robotics Corp.</p>
<p>-- New York newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
</text>
